Push Rules v1

PUSH-001 · Hard Fail · Push eligibility — audience must include one of:
CORE_PUSH_OPTED_IN_IOS | CORE_PUSH_OPTED_IN_ANDROID | CORE_PUSH_OPTED_IN_ALL_PLATFORMS
OR push gate = "Opted-in users only"

PUSH-002 · Warn · Platform targeting alignment:
· Name/tags indicate iOS-only → segment must target iOS only (_ios in segment name)
· Name/tags indicate Android-only → segment must target Android only (_android in segment name)
· Segment does not clearly match indicated platform → Warn
· Platform intent cannot be determined → Warn, confirm with campaign owner

PUSH-003 · Hard Fail · Platform asset verification per message step:
· iOS-only indicated → only APNs assets present. Android (FCM) present = Hard Fail
· Android-only indicated → only FCM assets present. iOS (APNs) present = Hard Fail
· Both platforms intended or no restriction → both assets expected, no finding
· Platform intent cannot be determined → To Be Checked

PUSH-004 · Hard Fail · Default KVP values must be present in every push message:
· key1 = value1
· key2 = value2
Hard Fail if either KVP is missing or value does not match exactly.

CLICK-001 · Warn · On-click behaviour:
· Set to "Open app" with no deeplink or URL → Warn
· Confirm with campaign owner whether deeplink or web URL should be added

CHECKPOINT · Confirm: say "Push block fully loaded"
